\p{These notes are based on lectures given by Dr [[EGR0]] for MA-663 at [[\stevensinstitute]].}

\p{We discuss the mathematical theory of learning. Our goal is to define and build models of learning, and prove statements about optimal efficiency.}

\p{We will describe the intuitive notions of “problem” and “algorithm” in a formal way. This is largely to illustrate that we can. In practice, intuition is more important than formality.}

